# Secret group `api`: alldots-api's own settings and secrets: setup token, listener, push, OAuth clients, public URL and outbound mail.
# Loaded by: alldots-api.service.
#
# Ownership and mode are load-bearing: `root:root 0600`. systemd reads EnvironmentFile= as root
# before dropping privileges. provision.sh installs this template to
# /opt/alldots/shared/env/api.env only when that file does not exist, so an operator's values are
# never overwritten by a rerun, and it never prints a value. A key belongs to exactly one group
# (docs/architecture/delivery-and-operations.md); this file is excluded from restic backups.
#
# `apns-key.p8` sits next to the group directory at `/opt/alldots/shared/apns-key.p8`,
# `root:alldots 0640`: the `alldots` service user reads it directly by path. Apple issues APNs auth
# keys as a `.p8` file, and a multi-line PEM has no safe representation as one `KEY=VALUE` line in
# an `EnvironmentFile=`, so it is distributed as its own file.

# SETUP_TOKEN: one-time bootstrap secret for POST /api/setup on alldots-api. Generate with:
# openssl rand -hex 32
SETUP_TOKEN=

# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY / VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY / VAPID_SUBJECT: generate the key pair with
# `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`. VAPID_SUBJECT is a mailto: or https: URL identifying this
# deployment's operator, per the Web Push protocol.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
VAPID_SUBJECT=

# APNS_TEAM_ID / APNS_KEY_ID / APNS_TOPIC: from the Apple Developer account's APNs auth key and
# the app's bundle id. APNS_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH points at the `.p8` file distributed alongside this
# one — see the header note.
APNS_TEAM_ID=
APNS_KEY_ID=
APNS_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/opt/alldots/shared/apns-key.p8
APNS_TOPIC=

# GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID / GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET: Google Cloud OAuth client for Gmail API mail
# sync (mailSyncJob.ts's "gmail_api" mode). Read by alldots-api's Gmail sync transport
# (backend/services/alldots-api/src/mailSyncAdapters.ts). If either is empty, alldots-api starts,
# logs one warning, and Gmail-mode accounts fail to sync. The same client signs a user in when a Gmail
# mailbox is connected (POST /api/mail/mailboxes/oauth/start): register
# <APP_BASE_URL>/api/mail/oauth/callback as its redirect URI. Without the client that route answers 500.
# The client's OAuth consent screen (Google Cloud > Google Auth Platform > Data access) must list the
# scopes the sign-in asks for: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.modify,
# https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send and, for Calendars, https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.
GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# GMAIL_PUBSUB_TOPIC / GMAIL_PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION / GMAIL_PUBSUB_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_PATH: Gmail push for
# gmail_api accounts. Read by alldots-api's Gmail watch hosting (backend/services/alldots-api/src/gmailPubSubConfig.ts).
# GMAIL_PUBSUB_TOPIC is the already-provisioned Cloud Pub/Sub topic `users.watch` publishes to, as
# projects/<project>/topics/<topic>; GMAIL_PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION is its pull subscription, as
# projects/<project>/subscriptions/<subscription>. GMAIL_PUBSUB_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_PATH is the path to
# the application's own Google service account JSON key, which authenticates the Pub/Sub calls (a user's
# Gmail grant has no Pub/Sub scope); alldots-api reads it once at startup and never logs it. Keep the key
# file outside this file, readable by the alldots service user only. If any of the three, or the Gmail
# OAuth client above, is empty, alldots-api starts, logs one warning, and Gmail accounts are synced by the
# periodic sweep only.
GMAIL_PUBSUB_TOPIC=
GMAIL_PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION=
GMAIL_PUBSUB_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_PATH=

# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_WEBHOOK_ENABLED: `true` lets alldots-api open Google Calendar push channels (`events.watch`) to
# <APP_BASE_URL>/api/calendar/google/webhook, read by backend/services/alldots-api/src/calendarPushComposition.ts.
# Google accepts them only for a domain verified for the Gmail OAuth client's project, so it is off unless set;
# without it Google calendars are synced by the periodic calendar sweep only.
GOOGLE_CALENDAR_WEBHOOK_ENABLED=

# MS_GRAPH_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID / MS_GRAPH_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET: Microsoft Entra app registration for
# Graph API mail sync (mailSyncJob.ts's "graph_api" mode). Read by alldots-api's Graph sync transport
# (backend/services/alldots-api/src/mailSyncAdapters.ts). If either is empty, alldots-api starts,
# logs one warning, and Graph-mode mail accounts fail to sync. The same registration signs a user in when
# an Outlook mailbox is connected (POST /api/mail/mailboxes/oauth/start): register
# <APP_BASE_URL>/api/mail/oauth/callback as its redirect URI. Without it that route answers 500.
# Its delegated Microsoft Graph API permissions: Mail.ReadWrite, Mail.Send, offline_access, User.Read
# and, for Calendars, Calendars.ReadWrite.
MS_GRAPH_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
MS_GRAPH_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# PORT: the port alldots-api listens on. Must match deploy/Caddyfile's
# `reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080` — the same way ALLDOTS_DOMAIN (monitor.env) is also what
# provision.sh hands to Caddy through /etc/caddy/alldots.env.
PORT=8080

# TRUST_PROXY: alldots-api listens on loopback behind Caddy on the same host (deploy/Caddyfile),
# so every request's socket peer is 127.0.0.1. TRUST_PROXY=1 makes it read the last
# X-Forwarded-For hop (the one Caddy appends) as the client address for login throttling.
# Must be 1 in every deployment provisioned from deploy/; any other value means the header is ignored.
TRUST_PROXY=1

# APP_BASE_URL: read only by alldots-api. The public origin every emailed link (password reset,
# invitations) is built against. Must be https://<ALLDOTS_DOMAIN> with no path. An absent value
# means http://localhost:3000; an empty one breaks every link.
APP_BASE_URL=

# SMTP_HOST: read only by alldots-api. The outbound mail relay; it must be reachable from this host.
# Mail is sent only when both SMTP_HOST and SMTP_FROM_ADDRESS are set; otherwise password-reset
# requests still answer 200 but nothing is sent.
SMTP_HOST=

# SMTP_PORT: read only by alldots-api. The relay's port. Non-empty on purpose: an empty value
# fails startup once SMTP is configured.
SMTP_PORT=587

# SMTP_SECURE: read only by alldots-api. true means implicit TLS (port 465); any other value
# means a plain connection upgraded with STARTTLS where the relay offers it.
SMTP_SECURE=false

# SMTP_FROM_ADDRESS: read only by alldots-api. The sender address of every outbound mail. Needed
# together with SMTP_HOST to send mail at all.
SMTP_FROM_ADDRESS=

# SMTP_USER: read only by alldots-api. The relay login; credentials are sent only when it is set.
SMTP_USER=

# SMTP_PASSWORD: read only by alldots-api. A secret. Sent only when SMTP_USER is set.
SMTP_PASSWORD=
